We have origin_availability_node_linked already true (init). Need destination_availability_node_linked also true (init). So we can activate nodes after preparing and linking task_profile.

We also need to ensure nodes not occupied initially; they are not.

Thus after preparing, we assign operator, activate node, then lock availability.

Locking also requires origin_node_ready (or destination_node_ready) and not locked.

After lock, we get origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed (effects). Similarly for destination.

